From 3f472064a81440753ab736c9e3c96af7e0d79523 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:38:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Input: pm8xxx-vibrator - replace drive bits when
 intensity changes

The cached drive value retains the previous field. ORing in a new
level leaves old bits set when intensity decreases while enabled;
changing code 24 to 17 can instead program 25.

Clear the previous field before inserting the new level, preserving
unrelated bits. Refresh Timothy Schmidt's existing Fx0 fix onto the
verified current input-next source.

Codex (GPT-6) assisted the port and expanded actual-source sanitizer
model. With the complete series, the ascending/descending speed checks
pass; reverting field replacement fails 15232 checks. Native ARM/ARM64
vibrator and FF-helper objects compile with W=1 and no diagnostics.
Core regmap/work services are modeled; full FF IOCTL behavior and
physical acceptance of this current source remain unqualified.

Fixes: 11205bb63e5c ("Input: add support for pm8xxx based vibrator driver")

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c b/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
index e1d69089d4bd..d4fdb5652584 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
@@ -107,7 +107,8 @@ static int pm8xxx_vib_set(struct pm8xxx_vib *vib, bool on)
 		vib->level /= VIB_PER_STEP_mV(vib);
 
 	if (on)
-		val |= (vib->level << regs->drv_shift) & regs->drv_mask;
+		val = (val & ~regs->drv_mask) |
+		      ((vib->level << regs->drv_shift) & regs->drv_mask);
 	else
 		val &= ~regs->drv_mask;
 
